
⏺ This is a Supabase configuration issue. You need to enable Google and GitHub OAuth providers in your Supabase dashboard.

  Enable OAuth Providers in Supabase

  1. Go to Supabase Dashboard → Your project → Authentication → Providers
  2. For Google:
    - Click on Google
    - Toggle Enable Sign in with Google
    - Add your Client ID and Client Secret from https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
    - Set the redirect URL in Google Console to: https://<your-project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
  3. For GitHub:
    - Click on GitHub
    - Toggle Enable Sign in with GitHub
    - Add your Client ID and Client Secret from https://github.com/settings/developers
    - Set the callback URL in GitHub to: https://<your-project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback

  Quick Setup Links

  - Google OAuth: Create credentials at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials → Create OAuth 2.0 Client ID
  - GitHub OAuth: Create an OAuth App at https://github.com/settings/developers

  For both, the Authorized redirect URI / Callback URL should be:
  https://<your-supabase-project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback

  You can find your project ref in your Supabase URL (it's the subdomain part).